 Suppose that $\angle ADE=x$, so $\angle EDC=180^\circ-2x$.  Also, since triangle $BEC$ is isosceles, $\angle EBC=\angle ECB=90^\circ-\angle BCA=90^\circ-2\angle EDC=(3x-90)^\circ$.  Because $AED$ is isosceles, $\angle AED=180^\circ-2x$ and $\angle CEB=180^\circ-(3x-90)=(270^\circ-3x)^\circ$.  The sum of all four angles is $360^\circ$, so \begin{align*}
360^\circ&=(180^\circ-2x)+(180^\circ-2x)+(270^\circ-3x)\\
180^\circ&=x,
