 The determinant of the matrix is 0, which means
\[0 = \begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{pmatrix} = a(c^2 - ab) + b(a^2 - bc) + c(b^2 - ac) = 0.\]This expands as $a^3 + b^3 + c^3 - 3abc = 0.$  We can factor this as
\[(a + b + c)(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 - ab - ac - bc) = 0.\]If $a + b + c = 0,$ then
\[\frac{a}{b + c} + \frac{b}{a + c} + \frac{c}{a + b} = \frac{a}{-a} + \frac{b}{-b} + \frac{c}{-c} = \boxed{-3}.\] Otherwise, $a^2 + b^2 + c^2 - ab = ac - bc.$  After subtracting $c^2 + bc$ from both sides, we have
\[a^2 + b^2 - ac - bc = (a - b)(a - c) = 0,\]so $a = b,$ $a = c,$ or $b = c.$

If $a = b,$ then
\[\frac{a}{b + c} + \frac{b}{a + c} + \frac{c}{a + b} = 1 + \frac{c}{2a}.\]Squaring and pluggingback in gives $4a^2 c^2 + 4a^4 = 0.$  This equation has no real roots.

If $a = c,$ then
\[\frac{a}{b + c} + \frac{b}{a + c} + \frac{c}{a + b} = 1 + \frac{b}{2a},\]and squaring and plugging back in gives $4a^2 b^2 + 4ab^4 = 0.$  This equation has no real roots.

Finally, if $b = c,$ then
\[\frac{a}{b + c} + \frac{b}{a + c} + \frac{c}{a + b} = 1 + \frac{2b}{a + b},\]and squaring and plugging back in gives $a^2 + 4ab = 0.$  The only solution is $a = c,$ and we have already shown that this will lead to no possible values of $a,$ $b,$ $c.$

Thus, the possible values of the expression are $\boxed{-3}.$  Note that we can check that this is achievable for example by
\[\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}.\][asy]
unitsize(0.1cm);
